course: dictionary
lesson: 5477
title: A friendly word: lass
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lass is a girl or young woman. People in Scotland, Ireland and the north of England use it every day, and it goes with lad, which means boy.
explain: Lass can also be a friendly way to talk to a girl or woman. «Thanks, lass» is warm, like saying thanks, love, and it is not rude. Look at the clues: who is speaking, where they are, and how the words sound.
explain: Dialect words belong to a place, so they can sound strange somewhere else. In old songs, a lad and a lass fall in love, and a bonny lass is a pretty girl. Read the whole sentence, then decide what fits.
fact: Lass means girl or young woman.
fact: Lass is informal, and it is most common in Scotland, Ireland and the north of England.
fact: «Thanks, lass» is a friendly way to speak to a girl or woman.
fact: «The lass what helped me» is dialect; in standard English it is «the girl who helped me».
fact: Slang is regional too: «lass» means girl in Yorkshire and Scotland, «peng» means really good in London, and «rizz» means charm.
exercise: Tam says, «Thanks, lass» to a girl who held the door open. What does lass mean here? | A type of bread | A rude word for a boy | *A friendly way to speak to a girl or woman | A kind of farm animal
exercise: In Yorkshire, a friend says, «That lass is my cousin.» Who is the lass? | A grown-up man | A pet rabbit | A teacher | *A girl
exercise: In «the lass what helped me», which word is the dialect word for «who»? | me | helped | lass | *what
test: In an old song, a lad and a lass fall in love. Who are they? | Two cats | *A boy and a girl | A farmer and a horse | Two teachers
test: Which word means girl in Yorkshire slang? | rizz | ag | peng | *lass
exam: In «Thanks, lass, that was kind», what does lass show? | A rude word for a dog | A type of cake | *A friendly word for a girl or woman | A name for a car
